##
## Interface labels. Doxia Sitetools 2.0 gives a skin no message bundle of its own ($text reads
## only the site renderer's bundle, and a bundle inside the skin jar fails the build), so a site
## overrides the English below with <custom><supaSkin><labels><key>text</key></labels>. Keys are
## flat camelCase names: Doxia cannot reach an element name that contains a dot. The key set and
## the English defaults live only here (the scripts keep their own copies of the keys they use);
## the reference table is "Labels" in src/site/markdown/configuration.md. Values are plain text,
## always HTML-escaped, and {name} placeholders are filled in by the skin. A key marked true is
## also read by the scripts, which receive an overridden value as data-supa-label-<kebab-key>.
#macro( supaDefineLabel $key $english $script )
#set( $_ = $supaLabelDefaults.put( $key, $english ) )
#if( $script )
#set( $_ = $supaScriptLabelKeys.add( $key ) )
#end
#end
